    "question": {
      ":question/id": "fba1b1c0-5b87-50fd-be09-4ef573df8b90",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+14y-6z &=-10 \\\\ x+7y-3z &=-5 \\\\ 2x+14y-6z &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 14 & -6 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 14 & -6 & -10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1\\leftrightarrow R_2\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 7 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 14 & -6 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 14 & -6 & -10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(-2)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 7 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 14 & -6 & -10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(-2)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 7 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n",
